  "style": {
    "01_register": "UI labels: concise modern Simplified Chinese, Koei RTK terminology, no articles or filler. Narrative text (bios, rumors, events, logs, battle text): elegant, lightly classical wuxia prose (古风白话), four-character phrases and parallelism welcome, but readable; avoid heavy 文言, internet slang and modern bureaucratic words (e.g. 赤脚医生, 山寨 as 'knock-off').",
    "02_ui_length": "Buttons, tabs and labels ideally <= 8 characters (most 2-4). Short stat names are exactly 2 characters and identical to the long ones: 武力 统率 智力 政治 魅力. Prefer verb-object labels (征兵, 读档, 结束回合).",
    "03_punctuation": "Full-width Chinese punctuation in text (，。：；！？（）、); quotes “ ” with ‘ ’ nested; ellipsis …… (English '...' as in 'Recruit...' becomes 登用……). Keep ASCII for placeholders, numbers, %, /, x, +, - signs in values (e.g. 士气+{amount}, {value} / {max}, 1x). English ' - ' separators in UI lines may become ' · ' or '，'. Runs of spaces separating fields in English UI lines also become ' · ' (士气{morale} · 训练{training}; 金钱：{gold} · 兵粮：{food}). Column sort indicators: ascending ↑, descending ↓ (never a Latin v or ^).",
    "04_placeholders": "Never translate or rename {placeholders}; keep the same set, reorder freely. No spaces around placeholders in CJK text (率兵{troops}自{city}出发). Faction placeholders: drop the English article ('the {faction}' -> '{faction}'). Do not attach gendered pronouns to officer placeholders; repeat the placeholder or use 其/此人.",
    "05_numbers_units": "Gold after a number: {n}金 (花费{cost}金, 金钱{gold} as a label). Food: 兵粮{n} (or {n}兵粮); troops: label 兵力{n}, in prose 率兵{troops} / {troops}兵马, counted men {count}名士兵. Percent stays {chance}%. Days: {days}日; months: {months}个月.",
    "06_dates": "Year {year}, Month {month}, Day {day} -> {year}年{month}月{day}日; '({season})' -> （{season}）; battle 'Day {day}' -> 第{day}日; 'Day {day} of {days}' -> 第{day}/{days}日; log date {year}.{month} keeps its dots.",
    "07_names": "Proper names come from the scenario nameZh fields (see 'names'); never transliterate pinyin. Han names are written without spaces or middle dots, including compound surnames (赫连勃, 拓跋鹰, 慕容啸, 独孤衡, 上官秋, 欧阳慈, 司徒康, 东方策, 南宫烈). Cities by their nameZh only (Yanmen Pass city label = 雁门; in narrative prose 'Yanmen Pass' may be 雁门关, 'Jade Gate' = 玉门关).",
    "08_epithets": "Epithets ('names' officer.*.epithet) are 绰号 without the English article. Display pattern '{name}, {epithet}' -> “{epithet}”{name} (e.g. “赤缨”燕红缨, “渊鉴”屈镜渊). When prose refers to someone by epithet (the Grey Wolf, the Quick Knife), reuse the same 绰号 (苍狼, 快刀). An epithet is a sobriquet, not a weapon name or a word-for-word calque: avoid modern associations (红缨枪 evokes the 儿童团/民兵 spear) and ominous calques (深渊 for 'Abyss').",
    "09_factions": "Faction names exactly as in 'names': 铁旗军, 西狼骑, 青庭, 东海盟, 南莲, 黑山寨. Short references: 'the League' = 东海盟, 'the Brotherhood' = 黑山寨, 'the Court' = 青庭. Banner glyphs stay the single characters 燕 赫 刘 沈 苏 墨. Independent cities: 独立 / 独立势力. Several faction names already end in a military noun (铁旗军, 西狼骑, 黑山寨), so never append 军 to {faction}: a faction's army on the map is {faction}部队.",
    "10_address": "Subordinates address the player ruler as 主公; Liu Chengxuan as 殿下; Helian Bo as 大汗 (third person 可汗); Su Wanqing as 主上 (third person 女王); Black Mountain sworn brothers say 大哥. Exception: commoners who are not the ruler's retainers (the tavern innkeeper in ui.strategy.noRumor) say 大人 and may use 您. Player-facing logs and hints use 我方/我军 for 'your/our' rather than 你/您 (我军 only in military contexts; the ruler's house as a whole, e.g. refusing alms, is 我方); system messages may simply omit the subject (仅可在筹划阶段存档). 主公 is only for speech or UI addressed to the player; third-person narration (bios, rumors, descriptions) says 主君 / 自家主君 or names the ruler. Reports addressed to the player keep the vocative of the English ('My lord {ruler}, ...' -> 主公{ruler} / 主公).",
    "11_pronouns_gender": "Female officers (use 她 in bios/rumors where a pronoun is needed): 燕红缨、赫连月、林霜月、上官秋、徐莫愁、沈玉珠、程兰茵、苏婉卿、江小蛮、范青芝、宁书玉、乔银铃、姚素、欧阳慈、云飞雪、萧琴音、兰月如、叶知秋、陆晨曦、何云裳. All others are male (他).",
    "12_battle_locations": "battle.location.* are inserted into {location} in other sentences, so translate them as place noun phrases: 'Road to {city}' -> {city}郊外 (never {city}道: 河东道 is the Tang Hedong Circuit and 东海道 reads as Japan's Tōkaidō), 'Siege of {city}' -> {city}城下, 'the battlefield' -> 战场; then 'The battle of {location}' -> {location}之战 (洛京郊外之战), 'at {location}' -> 于{location} (于洛京郊外). log.battle.field ('on the road to {city}') uses the same 于{city}郊外. Because {location} may be {city}城下 (the attackers' ground outside the walls), battle summaries use {location} only as the scene of the battle ({location}之战, 于{location}得胜/断粮, 兵临{location}) and never make the defender hold {location}; they may open with {location}之战 or with 第{day}日. 'X holds the field' = X占据战场 (not 据守, which means defending a fortified position).",
    "13_duel": "Duel / Single Combat = 一骑讨 in UI and logs (挑战 for the challenge, 应战 to accept). Moves: Strike 猛击, Feint 虚招, Guard 格挡; rule line: 猛击克虚招，虚招克格挡，格挡克猛击. Technique = 绝技; '{technique} ({move})' keeps the brackets as full-width （）.",
    "14_orders_vs_stats": "Keep the order/attribute pairing consistent: 开垦农田 -> 农业, 振兴商业 -> 商业, 修补城墙 -> 城防, 巡察 -> 治安, 征兵 -> 兵力, 训练士兵 -> 训练, 门派修行 -> 武力经验, 赠礼 -> 信任. Order previews read as '<attribute>+{amount}' (农业+{amount}).",
    "15_phases": "Planning phase = 筹划阶段 (labels: {season} · 筹划); the month playing out = 行动阶段 / 本月进行中. End Turn = 结束回合 on both the strategy and the battle screen. Delegate = 委任 (city to a governor, battle to the generals); Take Command / Command button = 亲自指挥.",
    "16_wuxia_world": "Sect = 门派, sect master = 掌门, Moonwell's mistress = 堂主, abbot = 方丈, disciples = 弟子. The world: 九州 (Nine Provinces), 天下 (the realm), 天命 (the Mandate), 幼帝 (boy emperor), 先帝 (old emperor), 朝廷 (the court), 大河 (Great River), 南江 (Southern River), 中原 (Central Plain).",
    "17_region_labels": "Map region labels 东海 and 黑山 coincide with the city names 东海 (Donghai) and 黑山 (Heishan) by design: the English pinyin city names literally mean those regions.",
    "18_consistency": "Use exactly one rendering per English term across all four chunks (see 'terms'; parenthesised notes in the English keys disambiguate senses, e.g. Command (stat) 统率 vs Take Command 亲自指挥). Do not invent alternative names for people, places, factions, sects or techniques.",
    "19_logs": "Chronicle logs report a changed value as 提升至{value} (增至 for troop counts; 已达 when the value may be unchanged, e.g. Martial after sect training); avoid the calque 现为. Logs use narrative verbs (调往, not the UI command 移动至). 'Already at maximum' order validation messages use one form: X已达上限 / X已开发至上限."
  },
